**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`

**How to implement.** MuellerInverseTests' quartz ground truth and its C1-C4 measurement design move into `BerremanTestSupport`, so the Planner's acceptance facts (step 475) read the design instead of transcribing it (the S14.1 brief 'Acceptance REUSES the existing facts' designs and helpers … Move a design definition into BerremanTestSupport if a fact needs it outside its class'; 001 §M 'Their designs and helpers are reused; no new physics test is written'; 001 §Q 'The ground truth and designs … move into a shared test-support project'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). The design moves whole, because C1-C4 is one table (specs/0044/.manual/004 §3.4) and the Planner's facts read C1, C3 and the full set. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step each moved name is declared once. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/QuartzSample.fs`, `module BerremanTestSupport.QuartzSample`, declared as `BiaxialSample.fs` is (step 345), appended at the end of `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. It receives from `MuellerInverseTests` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:waveLength` to `:fullConfigurations`), in this order and with their bodies and docs as S10.1 to S12.2 leave them: `waveLength`, `quartzOrdinaryIndex`, `quartzExtraordinaryIndex`, `quartzG11`, `quartzG33`, `quartz` (a `CrystalPhysics.UniaxialParameters`, step 353), `thickPlate`, `thinPlate`, `configuration` (over `MuellerFitting.configurationOf`, step 335), `c1`, `c2`, `c3`, `c4` and `fullConfigurations`, with the two banner comments above them (the quartz ground truth and its provenance; the C1-C4 measurement set and why each configuration exists); in the first banner 'Spec R3 puts the material in the TEST' becomes 'in test code', in the second 'the ablation fact below' (twice) becomes '`MuellerInverseTests`' ablation fact', and every other line keeps its text. It opens what they read (the engine's `Constants`, `Fields`, `MaterialProperties` and `Media`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics` and `MuellerInverse`, and `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting`), reads no name of the `BerremanTests` namespace, and its module doc says in one to three lines that it is spec 0044's quartz ground truth and its C1-C4 design, shared by `MuellerInverseTests` and the Planner's facts (spec 0050 S14.1). No reference is added: `BerremanTestSupport` already references Domain and Optimization (steps 344, 345). (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs` deletes those declarations and their banners and opens `BerremanTestSupport.QuartzSample` after its last `open`; every other binding (`degree`, `solverParameters`, `forward`, `observe`, `scalingAround`, `perturbedStart`, the boxes, the fit runners, `blindStart`, the noisy helpers) and every fact stays and reads the moved names unqualified; the class doc keeps its text. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): every expression is unchanged, and a module value is the value the class computed for every instance. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests`, the class whose design moved, is selected.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/QuartzSample.fs` MUST declare the quartz ground truth and the C1-C4 design once, every value unchanged, and `MuellerInverseTests` MUST read them from it and declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
